          "english_quote": "“The first group” and “the same” follow the printed conjectures compared with the versions. The reported Athos readings differ grammatically; “the same” replaces a reported phrase meaning “according to these.”",
          "issue": "Independently checked against the selected Greek and supplied apparatus, footnote b gives an incorrect meaning for the reported καὶ αὗται: it means “and these,” not “according to these.” It also characterizes πρώτοις versus προτέροις as a grammatical difference rather than the wording distinction “first” versus “former.” The simplified main text’s contextual reference to “the first group” is compatible with the selected source, but the note does not accurately disclose the reported readings.",
          "suggested_revision": "State that the selected Greek uses the conjectures προτέροις (“former ones,” rendered contextually here as “the first group”) and αἱ αὐταί (“the same”), whereas the apparatus reports Athos πρώτοις (“first ones”) and καὶ αὗται (“and these”). Remove “according to these” and avoid supplying an unsupported reconstruction of the alternative clause. Submit the revised note for fresh review.",
